      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.689,
            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 10:** A TV is bought at a price of ₹21,000. After 1 year, the value of the TV depreciates by 5%. Find the value of the TV after one year."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.144,
            0.494,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "The amount of reduction in the value is 5% of $\\begin{array} { r } { 2 1 \\mathrm { , } 0 0 0 = 0 . 0 5 \\times 2 1 \\mathrm { , } 0 0 0 } \\\\ { = 1 0 5 0 . } \\end{array}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.199,
            0.487,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "The current value is 21,000 – 1050 = 19,950."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.143,
            0.856,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "The value of the TV after 1 year will be 95% of the current value = 95% of 21,000 = 0.95 × 21,000 = 19,950."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.246,
            0.615,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "The value of the TV after 1 year will be ₹19,950."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.276,
            0.847,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 11:** The population of a village was observed to be reducing by about 10% every decade. If the current population is 1250, what is the expected population after 3 decades?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.351,
            0.473,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": "The population 1 decade later will be 0.9 times the population of the current decade."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.406,
            0.445,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the population after 1 decade will be 1250 × 0.9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.443,
            0.483,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "The population after 2 decades will be 1250 × 0.9 × 0.9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.48,
            0.483,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "The population after 3 decades will be $\\begin{array} { c } { { 1 \\bar { 2 } 5 \\bar { 0 } \\times 0 . 9 \\times 0 . 9 \\times 0 . 9 } } \\\\ { { = 9 1 1 . 2 5 . } } \\end{array}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.35,
            0.841,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": "First decade’s decrease = 0.1 × 1250 = 125."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.387,
            0.778,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { P o p u l a t i o n ~ a f t e r ~ 1 ~ d e c a d e } = 1 2 5 0 - 1 2 5 = 1 1 2 5 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_24_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.424,
            0.752,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "Second decade’s decrease"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.461,
            0.776,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { P o p u l a t i o n ~ a f t e r ~ 2 ~ d \\acute { e } c a d e s } \\atop = 1 1 2 5 - 1 1 2 = 1 0 1 3",
          "image_source": "images/page_24_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.498,
            0.844,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": "Third decade’s population decrease = 0.1 × 1013 = 101.3 ≅ 101."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.535,
            0.771,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "Population after 3 decades = 1013 – 101 = 912."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.578,
            0.846,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "Rounding off, we can say that the expected population after 3 decades will be around 910."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.632,
            0.389,
            0.654
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Tricky Percentages"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.663,
            0.36,
            0.683
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Would You Rather?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.693,
            0.749,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "？ You have won a contest. The organisers offer you two options to choose from:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.731,
            0.642,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "Option A: You deposit ₹100 and you get back ₹300."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.75,
            0.663,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "Option B: You deposit ₹1000 and you get back ₹1500."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.768,
            0.804,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "What is the percentage gain each option gives? You can choose any option only once. Which option would you choose? Why?"
        },
        {
